# If I had known in Russian: если бы я знал, я бы…
subtitle: "Если бы я знал, я бы пришёл: one Russian form for if I knew and if I had known, plus ли … или нет."
tags: ["russian","если бы","russian conditional","ли или","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/conditional-past","grammar/indirect-questions"]
thumb: "band \"If I had known, in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Two thirds and a million in Russian: fractions and per cent","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/176-russian-two-thirds.cast"}

